// Listeners' formats (DESIGN-COMPUTE §26.4-§26.8; LSTN-M13-01): the list a device publishes as its versionless
// s/<sidecar_id> in its network's listeners repo, and the live ask's bodies, LISTENERS and LISTENERS_RESULT (0x1901,
// 0x1902, §6.11, Appendix D), on the control-class contract any two admitted sidecars of a network hold (D-PROTO-18,
// D-LSTN-7). §26.6 writes the file as JSON whose fields are these, and §26.8 names the ask's fields without numbers:
// they take numbers in the order written (compute-plan-lstn-file-fields, QD-1249), the file's in its example's key
// order. The file itself is the JSON form listeners_file.go writes and reads, keys and enum values as named here, so
// it reaches EVS only sealed, a ciphertext evs sees with its writer, size and write time (§26.11, R-LSTN-7); the ask
// rides only Required-mode ciphertext between two sidecars. No server reads a field, so none takes a §2.8 row.
//
// The file carries no address of its host: readers take the host's overlay address and name from the config (§26.4).
// An entry's bind is a wildcard there, "0.0.0.0" or "::"; only an own-view entry, which reaches the host's person's own
